The D7 conditional monotonicity card says the F/W first variations are hypotheses (B-D7-F-DERIVATIVE, B-D7-W-FIRST-VARIATION). My task for D12-entropy-variation is to prove one missing analytic step: differentiation of time-dependent weighted integrals under explicit regularity/domination (Leibniz integral rule with time-dependent measure), or a concrete F/W derivative identity on a proved nontrivial model.

